WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.920
Hello and Merry Christmas. My name is Larry Arnn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.640
I work at Hillsdale College, and this&nbsp;
is the most important being on earth.&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.320
Her name is Charlotte, or we call her The&nbsp;
Squink, and she is our first grandchild.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.800
She seems a good thing to have around&nbsp;
here in a Christmas message because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.800
the Christmas message is about a baby, and&nbsp;
every baby represents something like Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:32.560
because babies are small, and yet everyone knows&nbsp;
they're of infinite value, certainly this one is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:40.960
Yes, so true. Think about the&nbsp;
Nativity story. Did you have to memorize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.400
Bible passages when you were young? I&nbsp;
did. Look at that, the star has fallen.&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:55.840
I had to memorize the Luke account of the&nbsp;
Nativity and I can remember most of it:  "And there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.760
were in the same country shepherds abiding&nbsp;
in the field watching their flocks by night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.720
And the angel of the Lord came upon them, and the glory of&nbsp;
the Lord shone about them..." —and this is the part I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:14.320
like— "...and they were sore afraid." So, what were they&nbsp;
afraid about and what did the angel come to say?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:28.160
This baby had been born, and the news of the baby&nbsp;
was so shocking that Herod killed many babies to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:36.000
make sure he got that one killed because that one&nbsp;
was going to challenge his rule. Well that one did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:43.680
challenge his rule, and the rule of every tyrant&nbsp;
in history because the Christmas message is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:54.960
nobody except God can have absolute power, and&nbsp;
nobody but God deserves it.  It's a very turbulent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:02.000
world right now. Our College is thriving. I
think that's because of help from people like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:09.280
you, but I think that's because we, together,&nbsp;
we remember that there are eternal things,&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:21.840
and one of the finest happened at Christmas, when&nbsp;
a baby was born. Thank you, and Merry Christmas.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.420
 

